AB  - Large language models (LLMs) have recently attracted significant attention for their potential in Verilog code generation. However, existing LLM-based methods face several challenges, including data scarcity and the high computational cost of generating prompts for fine-tuning. Motivated by these challenges, we explore methods to augment training datasets, develop more efficient and effective prompts for fine-tuning, and implement training methods incorporating electronic design automation (EDA) tools. Our proposed framework for fine-tuning LLMs for Verilog code generation includes (1) abstract syntax tree (AST)-based data augmentation, (2) output-relevant code masking, a prompt generation method based on the logical structure of Verilog code, and (3) reinforcement learning with tool feedback (RLTF), a fine-tuning method using EDA tool results. Experimental studies confirm that our framework significantly improves syntax and functional correctness, outperforming commercial and non-commercial models on open-source benchmarks.
