AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable capabilities in code generation across various programming languages and domains. In this paper, we present the first empirical study investigating the use of LLMs for generating ATL (ATLAS Transformation Language) model transformation code in the context of Model-Driven Engineering (MDE). Through controlled experiments using minimal prompts and metamodels, we show that state-of-the-art LLMs such as ChatGPT and Claude can produce syntactically correct and executable ATL transformations. The results confirm that LLMs have implicitly learned ATL's structural and semantic patterns, enabling the automatic generation of valid transformation rules. This opens new research directions for the MDE community, suggesting that LLMs can serve as practical assistants or co-authors in building and validating model transformation solutions.
ER  - 

