AB  - Industrial Control Systems (ICS) increasingly require automated and high-assurance generation of IEC 61131-3 Structured Text (ST) code. Existing large-scale language models (LLMs) are too computationally demanding and lack the formal reliability for deployment on typical PLC hardware. To address this limitation, SLM4PLC introduces a correctness-by-construction (CbC) framework that leverages compact Small Language Models (SLMs) to synthesize formally verifiable ST code under strict industrial resource constraints. The proposed framework integrates Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Agentic RAG) with structured Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting to reduce reasoning errors, constrain safety-critical logic, and improve grounding in IEC 61131-3 programming patterns. A lightweight SLM, fine-tuned using QLoRA, serves as the code generation engine. Results demonstrate consistent improvements in syntactic validity, logical soundness, and formal verifiability, establishing that SLM4PLC delivers edge-deployable, formally guaranteed PLC code generation suitable for simulation and real industrial automation environments.
ER  - 

