AB  - Configuring Large Language Model (LLM) hyperparameters to balance accuracy and computational cost for code generation is a critical challenge. We propose a multi-objective optimization framework using the NSGA-II genetic algorithm to address this. The framework co-optimizes inference parameters and prompting strategies to simultaneously maximize code accuracy and minimize token consumption. Validated on the HumanEval benchmark across three LLMs (Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-Coder-7B, and Mistral-7B), our approach identified Pareto-optimal fronts that surpassed the accuracy of a sequential search baseline while reducing optimization time by 6 to 12 times. This work contributes a robust, automated framework for LLM tuning, providing practitioners with validated configurations for diverse operational constraints.
